---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components'
import DiagramLabel from './DiagramLabel.astro'

// The determinism kit, drawn for the engineer who pinned the model and is still chasing a flake.
// Determinism is a property of the WHOLE run: every nondeterministic source is pinned behind an
// injected port, the hermetic lane wires the frozen ones, a served run injects real ones at the same
// call site. The board lists each source and what pins it; the model is flagged as the loud one
// everyone stops at, and the scanners are flagged as the part a toy agent would never teach you.
//
// Every pin names a real symbol in the rebuilt tree:
//   harness/gateway.py   Gateway, Mode.REPLAY, CassetteMiss
//   harness/sources.py   FrozenClock, SystemClock, IdFactory, SpanSequence, FIXTURE_INSTANT
//   harness/egress.py    block_egress, EgressBlocked  (patches socket.connect and friends)
//   tests/test_determinism.py  the two AST scanners, over the whole runtime tree
// The RNG row is deliberately not "seed 0". Nothing in the tree owns a global seed; the rule is that
// a runtime path may never touch the process wide `random`, and the two modules that do use `random`
// build their own local `random.Random(...)`. That rule is enforced by an AST scanner, not by trust.

const sources = [
  { src: 'the model', pin: 'Gateway · REPLAY · miss = hard fail', icon: 'material-symbols:smart-toy-outline', loud: true },
  { src: 'the clock', pin: 'FrozenClock · now never moves', icon: 'material-symbols:schedule-outline' },
  { src: 'the RNG', pin: 'a local random.Random, never the global', icon: 'material-symbols:casino-outline' },
  { src: 'ids + refs', pin: 'IdFactory · derived, not UUIDs', icon: 'material-symbols:tag' },
  { src: 'span order', pin: 'SpanSequence · never the clock', icon: 'material-symbols:sort' },
  { src: 'network egress', pin: 'block_egress · a socket raises', icon: 'material-symbols:lan-outline' },
]
---

<div class="not-prose my-10 border border-border-dark bg-surface rounded-lg overflow-hidden" data-dk>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-3 bg-surface-container-high border-b border-border-dark flex-wrap">
    <DiagramLabel icon="material-symbols:lock-clock-outline" label="The determinism kit · pin more than the model" />
    <span class="dk-note">every unpinned source is a red that comes and goes</span>
  </div>

  <div class="p-5 flex flex-col gap-0">
    <div class="dk-grid">
      {
        sources.map((s) => (
          <div class:list={['dk-cell', s.loud && 'dk-loud']}>
            <span class="dk-src"><Icon name={s.icon} class="text-[14px] text-primary" />{s.src}</span>
            <span class="dk-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="material-symbols:lock-outline" class="text-[12px]" /></span>
            <span class="dk-pin">{s.pin}</span>
            {s.loud && <span class="dk-flag">loudest · pinned first, last responsible</span>}
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="dk-trap">
      <span class="dk-trap-h"><Icon name="material-symbols:warning-outline" class="text-[14px]" />the trap the list cannot catch</span>
      <span class="dk-trap-b">
        A board like this decays the moment someone adds a source it does not name. So the ban is not a
        convention, it is <b>two AST scanners over the whole runtime tree</b>: one for wall clock reads, one
        for calls into the process wide <code>random</code>. The clock scanner asserts <b>equality</b> with its
        allowlist, so a stale exemption fails as loudly as a new read and cannot outlive the code it names.
        Both scanners are pointed at a synthetic violation first, because a detector nobody proved can detect
        is just a green test.
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="dk-legend">
      Pin the agent by pinning its <b>ports</b>: the chat model the graph calls, the tools it invokes, the
      clock it reads, the sockets it may not open. More work than a toy loop, and far more credible, because
      real teams ship on frameworks and this tests what you actually deploy.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style is:global>
  [data-dk] .dk-note { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  [data-dk] .dk-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { [data-dk] .dk-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  [data-dk] .dk-cell {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark); background: var(--color-surface-container-low);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-loud {
    grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr;
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 40%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 5%, transparent);
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-src {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-arrow { color: var(--color-text-muted); display: inline-flex; }
  [data-dk] .dk-pin { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.66rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); text-align: right; }
  [data-dk] .dk-flag {
    grid-column: 1 / -1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--color-primary); margin-top: 0.1rem;
  }

  [data-dk] .dk-trap {
    margin-top: 0.85rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-error) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-error) 5%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-trap-h {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.66rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-trap-b { font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--color-text-primary); line-height: 1.5; }
  [data-dk] .dk-trap-b b { font-weight: 600; }
  [data-dk] .dk-trap-b code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.92em; }

  [data-dk] .dk-legend {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  [data-dk] .dk-legend b { color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
</style>
